OpenJDK Mobile / HotSpot Zero runtime

The iOS runtime is built from OpenJDK Mobile:
  https://github.com/openjdk/mobile
  commit pinned by fetch-openjdk.sh (JDK 28)

- libjvm.a is HotSpot Zero (interpreter only), distributed under the GNU
  General Public License version 2 only, without the Classpath Exception.
- The class library (libjava, libzip, libnet, libnio, libjimage, libmanagement,
  libmanagement_ext and the jlinked modules) is GPL-2.0 with the Classpath
  Exception.
- An application that links libjvm.a is a GPLv2 combined work. Complete
  corresponding source is this repository (fetch-openjdk.sh,
  build-openjdk-ios.sh, package.sh and the application source) together with
  openjdk/mobile at the commit above. package.sh bundles OpenJDK's LICENSE,
  ASSEMBLY_EXCEPTION, ADDITIONAL_LICENSE_INFO and a SOURCE.md saying this.

Build prerequisites that are not part of the shipped runtime:
- libffi for iOS, from the ios-tools "libffi-build" release
  (https://github.com/openjdk-mobile/ios-tools/releases/tag/libffi-build),
  SHA-256 pinned in fetch-openjdk.sh; MIT licensed, licence bundled.
- A macOS JDK built from the same openjdk/mobile commit by
  build-openjdk-macos.sh, used only for its jmod and jlink tools (jlink
  requires modules and tools from the same JDK build). Not linked into the app.

No prebuilt VM archive is downloaded; the runtime is compiled from the pinned
openjdk/mobile source by this repository's scripts.
